window.HHA_FAQ=[["Èske gen yon egzamen leta pou HHA?","Is there a state HHA exam?","Pa gen yon sèl egzamen nasyonal. Règ federal la (42 CFR 484.80) mande yon evalyasyon konpetans, men se ajans lan oswa pwogram fòmasyon an ki fè l. Kèk eta gen pwòp règ yo. Nan Massachusetts, nou poko konfime yon règ leta separe: mande ajans oswa lekòl ou.","There is no single national exam. The federal rule (42 CFR 484.80) requires a competency evaluation, but the agency or training program runs it. Some states add their own rules. For Massachusetts, we have not confirmed a separate state rule: ask your agency or school.",["S6","S12"]],["Kisa evalyasyon konpetans lan gen ladan?","What does the competency evaluation include?","De pati: yon tès ekri oswa oral sou 14 sijè yo, ak konpetans pratik yon enfimyè (RN) gade w fè ak yon kliyan oswa yon moun k ap jwe wòl kliyan. Konpetans pratik yo se: kominikasyon, siy vital, ijyèn pèsonèl, transfè ak mache, ak ranje mouvman ak pozisyon.","Two parts: a written or oral test on the 14 subjects, and hands-on skills a registered nurse watches you do with a client or a person playing the client. The hands-on skills are: communication, vital signs, personal hygiene, transfers and walking, and range of motion and positioning.",["S6","S12"]],["Kisa k rive si m echwe yon konpetans?","What happens if I fail a skill?","Ou pa ka fè travay sa a san sipèvizyon dirèk jiskaske w fè fòmasyon ankò epi pase yon nouvo evalyasyon pou li. Si w echwe plis pase yon sijè obligatwa, ou pa konsidere kòm konpetan: ou dwe fè fòmasyon ankò epi pase evalyasyon an ankò.","You may not do that task without direct supervision until you are retrained and pass a new evaluation for it. If you fail more than one required area, you are not considered competent: you must be retrained and evaluated again.",["S6","S12"]],["Konbyen èdtan fòmasyon?","How many training hours?","Omwen 75 èdtan, ak omwen 16 èdtan klas anvan omwen 16 èdtan pratik sipèvize. Pati klas la ka fèt sou entènèt si l entèaktif. Kèk eta mande plis èdtan.","At least 75 hours, with at least 16 hours of classroom before at least 16 hours of supervised practical training. The classroom part can be online if it is interactive. Some states require more hours.",["S6","S12"]],["Konbyen tan sa pran?","How long does it take?","Règ federal la mande omwen 75 èdtan. Konbyen semèn sa pran depann de orè pwogram nan (plen tan oswa mwatye tan), kidonk mande pwogram nan.","The federal rule sets the minimum at 75 hours. How many weeks that takes depends on the program's schedule (full time or part time), so ask the program.",["S6"]],["Èske yon CNA ka travay kòm HHA?","Can a CNA work as an HHA?","Wi, dapre règ federal la, yon asistan enfimyè ki sou rejis leta a an règ ka kalifye kòm ed swen a domisil. Ajans lan ka toujou mande w fè yon evalyasyon sou travay lakay moun.","Yes. Under the federal rule, a nurse aide in good standing on the state registry can qualify as a home health aide. The agency may still ask you to show skills for home care.",["S6","S12"]],["Sètifika HHA sou entènèt: èske yo valab?","Online HHA certificates: are they valid?","Fè atansyon anvan w peye. Pou travay nan yon ajans Medicare, ou bezwen fòmasyon ak evalyasyon ki respekte 42 CFR 484.80, sa vle di ou dwe montre yon enfimyè (RN) konpetans ou an pèsòn. Mande ajans ou vle travay la ki pwogram li aksepte.","Be careful before you pay. To work for a Medicare agency, you need training and an evaluation that meet 42 CFR 484.80, including skills you show a registered nurse in person. Ask the agency you want to work for which programs it accepts.",["S6","S12"]],["Kisa m bezwen anvan m kòmanse?","What do I need before I start?","Sa varye selon pwogram ak ajans, e règ federal la pa bay yon sèl lis. Mande pwogram nan ak ajans lan egzijans egzak yo anvan w enskri.","It varies by program and agency, and the federal rule does not set one list. Ask the program and the agency for their exact requirements before you enroll.",["S6"]],["Kijan pou m rete kalifye?","How do I stay qualified?","Fè omwen 12 èdtan fòmasyon kontinyèl (in-service) chak 12 mwa. Si w pase 24 mwa youn apre lòt san w pa travay pou peye kòm ed, ou dwe fè fòmasyon ak evalyasyon ankò.","Complete at least 12 hours of in-service training every 12 months. If you go 24 months in a row without paid work as an aide, you must complete training and evaluation again.",["S6","S12"]],["Kijan app sa a ede m?","How does this app help?","Li kouvri 14 sijè federal yo, ak gid, kesyon ak kat konpetans pou chak. Li pa ranplase fòmasyon ofisyèl ou ni pratik ak yon enfimyè. Toujou swiv plan swen kliyan an ak règ ajans ou.","It covers all 14 federal subjects, with guides, questions and skill cards for each. It does not replace your official training or hands-on practice with a nurse. Always follow the client's care plan and your agency's rules.",["S6"]]];
